1.1.text:
Article 3

Protection of women from acts of violence aims to:
a. prevent violence against women;

• •
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women;
d. facilitate and mediate household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household;
e. provide services and/or handling to victims; and
f. empower women victims of violence and vulnerable groups.

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 28

1. The community participates in the implementation of women's protection.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:  a. establishing family partners at the sub-district/village level by the community;
b. establishing women's protection units in community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of women's rights;
d. taking preventive measures if indications of violence against women are found in the community;
e. providing first aid to victims; andf. reporting to the competent authorities if violence against women occurs in their environment.
3. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and/or mass media.

•  •

Article 23

Community and family have the obligation and responsibility to:
a. prevent the occurrence of violence against women;
b. report if violence occurs;
c. protect victims; andd. provide emergency assistance.

Article 5

1. Prevention efforts as referred to in Article 4 letter a shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the SKPD responsible for Women's Empowerment.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:a. establishing a working network;
b. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a violence prevention system;
d. disseminating laws and regulations related to the protection of women victims of violence, including raising awareness among families and communities;
e. providing education for women victims of violence including access to employment opportunities; andf. through complete and easily accessible communication, information and education media.
3. In addition to prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1), prevention efforts shall also be carried out by family and/or closest relatives, community, educational institutions and customary institutions.

CHAPTER III

VIOLENCE

Article 13

Violence against women consists of:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/orf. other violence.

Article 2

Protection of Women from acts of violence is based on:
a. respect and fulfillment of the rights of victims;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination; and d. the best interests of victims.

REGENT OF KUBU RAYA

PROVINCE OF WEST KALIMANTAN

REGIONAL REGULATION OF KUBU RAYA REGENCY NUMBER 9 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY THE REGENT OF KUBU RAYA, • • Considering Bearing in Mind
a. that violence against women constitutes a violation of human rights so that women need to be protected in their dignity and honor and their right to life must be guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny;
b. that to overcome violence against women in Kubu Raya Regency, prevention efforts and optimization of overcoming violence against women are needed through policies to guarantee legal protection for women;
c. that to provide legal protection for women, the regulation of protection of women from acts of violence needs to be regulated in a Regional Regulation;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b and c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women From Acts of Violence;
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 35 of 2007 concerning the Establishment of Kubu Raya Regency in West Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 101, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4751);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

• • With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF KUBU RAYA REGENCY and

Article 9

Empowerment as referred to in Article 4 letter c includes:
a. establishing communities of women victims of violence;
b. job training;
c. productive economic enterprises and joint business groups; and
d. capital assistance.

CHAPTER IV

RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 20

Every woman victim of violence has the right to:
a. have her dignity respected as a human being;
b. obtain physical and psychological health recovery from the suffering experienced;
c. determine her own decisions;
d. obtain information;
e. have her identity kept confidential;
f. obtain compensation;
g. obtain social rehabilitation;
h. obtain spiritual guidance;
1. obtain complaint handling;

J. obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
k. obtain assistance; and l. guarantee of rights related to status as a family member and community member.

Article 21

1. The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement victim protection efforts by:a. establishing PPT;
b. formulating policies;
c. preparing plans and implementing programs and activities;
d. providing facilities and infrastructure support; ande. supervising the implementation of services to victims with minimum service standards.

•  • (2) In implementing the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall prepare a Regional Action Plan for Women's Protection.

3. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 7

1. (2) • Forms of service and/or handling of victims include:
a. complaint handling including identification;
b. health/medical rehabilitation services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. law enforcement and legal aid services;
e. repatriation and social reintegration services; andf. psychological services.

Forms of service as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with Minimum Service Standards established by legislation implemented by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

